      "content": "I have the active MedicationRequests for Patient Jonathan Jackson (DOB 1984-11-03, MRN S1733937). Before I file anything to the chart, please confirm you want me to post the Observation summarized below for this patient.\n\nProposed Observation (draft; not yet posted)\n- Patient: Jonathan Jackson, DOB 1984-11-03, MRN S1733937\n- ResourceType: Observation\n- Status: final\n- Subject.reference: Patient/S1733937\n- Code.text: \"Medication reconciliation summary\"\n- effectiveDateTime: 2023-11-13T07:00:00Z\n- issued: 2023-11-13T07:00:00Z\n- valueString (narrative): see \u201cNarrative text\u201d below\n\nFull JSON payload I will post upon your confirmation:\n{\n  \"resourceType\": \"Observation\",\n  \"status\": \"final\",\n  \"category\": [\n    {\n      \"coding\": [\n        {\n          \"system\": \"http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-category\",\n          \"code\": \"vital-signs\",\n          \"display\": \"Vital Signs\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"code\": {\n    \"text\": \"Medication reconciliation summary\"\n  },\n  \"subject\": {\n    \"reference\": \"Patient/S1733937\"\n  },\n  \"effectiveDateTime\": \"2023-11-13T07:00:00Z\",\n  \"issued\": \"2023-11-13T07:00:00Z\",\n  \"valueString\": \"Medication reconciliation summary for active MedicationRequests\\n\\nGrouped by ingredient | form | route:\\n- Heparin | solution in NS | Apheresis: multiple active orders (10,000 U and 7,500 U variants); likely duplicates across sessions.\\n- Methoxsalen | injection solution | Other: multiple active orders associated with photopheresis; likely duplicates.\\n- Insulin lispro | solution | Subcutaneous: sliding-scale (NPO Q6H; bedtime mild/moderate) and prandial dosing (TID with meals, 6\u201312 U); concurrent orders present.\\n- Insulin NPH (isophane) | suspension | Subcutaneous: daily 6\u201323 U; duplicate entries present.\\n- Tacrolimus | 0.5 mg capsule | Oral: active orders include DAILY, QODAY, and day-of-week schedules; potential duplicate/conflicting orders.\\n- Valganciclovir | 450 mg tablet | Oral: QAM; duplicate entries present.\\n- Ferrous sulfate | 325 mg tablet | Oral: DAILY.\\n- Diltiazem HCl | 90 mg capsule (CP12) | Oral: DAILY; duplicate entries present.\\n- Mirtazapine | 45 mg tablet | Oral: QHS.\\n- Levofloxacin | 750 mg tablet | Oral: Q24H.\\n- Heparin, porcine (PF) | injection solution | Subcutaneous: pre-op once.\\n- Piperacillin\u2013tazobactam | IV solution | Intravenous: Q8H; two product variants active.\\n- Gadobutrol | IV solution | Intravenous: radiology once.\\n\\nComputed daily pill burden (solid oral dosage units/day):\\n- Tacrolimus 0.5 mg cap: 1\\n- Valganciclovir 450 mg tab: 1\\n- Ferrous sulfate 325 mg tab: 1\\n- Diltiazem HCl 90 mg cap (CP12): 1\\n- Mirtazapine 45 mg tab: 1\\n- Levofloxacin 750 mg tab: 1\\nTotal estimated solid oral pills per day: 6\\n\\nOther formulations (not included in pill count):\\n- Insulin lispro: up to TID with meals plus QHS sliding-scale; additional Q6H scale possible when NPO.\\n- Insulin NPH (isophane): typically once daily.\\n- Apheresis-related heparin and methoxsalen: administered per apheresis sessions.\\n- IV antibiotics/contrast as ordered.\\n\\nFlagged potential duplicates by ingredient:\\n- Heparin (apheresis solutions)\\n- Methoxsalen\\n- Insulin lispro\\n- Insulin NPH (isophane)\\n- Tacrolimus\\n- Valganciclovir\\n- Diltiazem HCl\\n- Piperacillin\u2013tazobactam\"\n}\n\nNarrative text (same as valueString to be filed)\nMedication reconciliation summary for active MedicationRequests\n\nGrouped by ingredient | form | route:\n- Heparin | solution in NS | Apheresis: multiple active orders (10,000 U and 7,500 U variants); likely duplicates across sessions.\n- Methoxsalen | injection solution | Other: multiple active orders associated with photopheresis; likely duplicates.\n- Insulin lispro | solution | Subcutaneous: sliding-scale (NPO Q6H; bedtime mild/moderate) and prandial dosing (TID with meals, 6\u201312 U); concurrent orders present.\n- Insulin NPH (isophane) | suspension | Subcutaneous: daily 6\u201323 U; duplicate entries present.\n- Tacrolimus | 0.5 mg capsule | Oral: active orders include DAILY, QODAY, and day-of-week schedules; potential duplicate/conflicting orders.\n- Valganciclovir | 450 mg tablet | Oral: QAM; duplicate entries present.\n- Ferrous sulfate | 325 mg tablet | Oral: DAILY.\n- Diltiazem HCl | 90 mg capsule (CP12) | Oral: DAILY; duplicate entries present.\n- Mirtazapine | 45 mg tablet | Oral: QHS.\n- Levofloxacin | 750 mg tablet | Oral: Q24H.\n- Heparin, porcine (PF) | injection solution | Subcutaneous: pre-op once.\n- Piperacillin\u2013tazobactam | IV solution | Intravenous: Q8H; two product variants active.\n- Gadobutrol | IV solution | Intravenous: radiology once.\n\nComputed daily pill burden (solid oral dosage units/day):\n- Tacrolimus 0.5 mg cap: 1\n- Valganciclovir 450 mg tab: 1\n- Ferrous sulfate 325 mg tab: 1\n- Diltiazem HCl 90 mg cap (CP12): 1\n- Mirtazapine 45 mg tab: 1\n- Levofloxacin 750 mg tab: 1\nTotal estimated solid oral pills per day: 6\n\nOther formulations (not included in pill count):\n- Insulin lispro: up to TID with meals plus QHS sliding-scale; additional Q6H scale possible when NPO.\n- Insulin NPH (isophane): typically once daily.\n- Apheresis-related heparin and methoxsalen: administered per apheresis sessions.\n- IV antibiotics/contrast as ordered.\n\nFlagged potential duplicates by ingredient:\n- Heparin (apheresis solutions)\n- Methoxsalen\n- Insulin lispro\n- Insulin NPH (isophane)\n- Tacrolimus\n- Valganciclovir\n- Diltiazem HCl\n- Piperacillin\u2013tazobactam\n\nAssumptions used for pill-burden/grouping\n- Counted only solid oral dosage units toward pill burden; injections/IV/contrast not counted but summarized.\n- When multiple active orders existed for the same ingredient/form/route, I treated them as potential duplicates and counted a single representative regimen for pill-burden purposes.\n- Tacrolimus: conflicting active sigs (DAILY, QODAY, day-of-week, and single-dose entries). Assumed 0.5 mg once daily for pill-burden estimation.\n- Insulin lispro: multiple concurrent sliding-scale and prandial orders; injection frequency not converted to \u201cpills\u201d; summarized qualitatively.\n- NPH insulin: summarized qualitatively as once daily based on active orders.\n- \u201cOnce,\u201d \u201cPre-op once,\u201d and \u201cRad once\u201d orders (e.g., heparin pre-op, gadobutrol) were not included in daily pill burden.\n- Diltiazem \u201cCP12\u201d treated as a single oral capsule daily.\n\nNext step\nPlease confirm: Post the above Observation to Patient/S1733937 as drafted? \n- If yes, I will file it now and return the created resource with its server-assigned id.\n- If you want any edits to the narrative or timing before posting, let me know and I will update before filing.",
