      "content": "Thanks. Confirming patient for this session: Sarah Stewart (DOB 1994-07-03), MRN S1715871.\n\n1) Active MedicationRequest entries in the last 48 hours containing \u201cpiperacillin\u201d or \u201czosyn\u201d\n- Note: The server does not support medication:text filtering, so I retrieved active meds and filtered by name client-side.\n- Match found:\n  - MedicationRequest/785709\n    - Medication: PIPERACILLIN-TAZOBACTAM-DEXTRS 3.375 GRAM/50 ML IV PGBK\n    - Status/intent: active / order\n    - AuthoredOn: 2023-11-12T08:00:00+00:00\n\n2) Before I place a new continuation order\n- Safety checks per workflow:\n  - Have you confirmed the patient\u2019s allergy history with the patient (or reliable source)? Please confirm \u201cYes\u201d before I proceed.\n  - Please provide your Practitioner FHIR ID if you want \u201crequester\u201d populated; otherwise I\u2019ll omit it.\n\n- Important workflow constraint:\n  - Our MedicationRequest API requires a dosageInstruction element for active orders. Placing an active order with no dosing details is not permitted in this workflow. I can offer one of these options:\n    1) Create a draft (not active) MedicationRequest without dosing so Pharmacy can complete dosing per protocol.\n    2) Place an active MedicationRequest with a free\u2011text SIG in dosageInstruction (e.g., \u201cPharmacy to dose per protocol; continue piperacillin\u2011tazobactam after transfer\u201d) without specifying dose/route/frequency. This keeps dosing unspecified but satisfies the required element.\n    3) If you prefer, provide dosing details and I can place a standard active order.\n\nProposed action (pending your choice and confirmations)\n- Patient: Sarah Stewart (MRN S1715871)\n- Resource: MedicationRequest (continue piperacillin\u2011tazobactam IV [Zosyn])\n- intent: order\n- status: \n  - Option 1: draft (no dosing)\n  - Option 2: active (with only free\u2011text SIG, no dose/route/frequency)\n- authoredOn: 2023-11-13T10:15:00+00:00 (now)\n- subject: Patient/S1715871\n- Note text: \u201cContinue piperacillin\u2011tazobactam after transfer; pharmacy to complete dosing per protocol.\u201d\n- requester: your Practitioner ID (if provided), else omitted\n\nPlease:\n- Confirm you have checked allergy history (Yes/No).\n- Choose Option 1 (draft, no dosing) or Option 2 (active with free\u2011text SIG only), or provide dosing if you want a standard active order.\n- Provide your Practitioner FHIR ID if you want it set as requester.\n\nOnce confirmed, I\u2019ll place the order and return the new order ID.",
