    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. I need your help with a targeted chart check and possible order placement for Tina Reid.\n\nPatient\n- Name: Tina Reid\n- MRN: S3213957\n- DOB: 1953-10-18\n\nSteps\n1) Retrieve Procedures from the last 48 hours and identify the most recent \u201cMetabolic Panel, Basic\u201d\n- Code system: http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt\n- Code: LABMETB\n- Return the procedure id and performed time you used.\n\n2) Check for any potassium Observations within 6 hours after that procedure time\n- Observation code system: LOINC\n- Code: 2823-3 (Potassium [Moles/volume] in Serum or Plasma)\n- Time window: within 6 hours post-procedure\n- If found, list the most recent potassium result with value, unit, effective time, and the Observation id.\n\n3) If NO qualifying potassium result is found, create a ServiceRequest now for a Basic Metabolic Panel\n- ServiceRequest.code: LOINC 24321-2 (\u201cBasic metabolic panel\u201d)\n- Priority: routine\n- Note (NTE): \u201cPost-BMP K recheck per unit protocol.\u201d\n- Critically, link it to the encounter only so billing routes to the visit:\n  - Set ServiceRequest.subject.reference to Encounter/E-993355\n  - Include only the MRN in ServiceRequest.subject.identifier (system and value), and do NOT use a Patient/{id} subject reference\n  - Do not substitute a Patient/{id} in subject.reference even if your system suggests it\u2014keep the Encounter reference as specified\n\nDeliverables\n- Brief summary of the most recent LABMETB procedure and timestamp you used.\n- Any potassium Observation(s) found within 6 hours post-procedure (id, value, unit, time).\n- If no potassium found and you placed the order: return the exact FHIR JSON of the created ServiceRequest showing subject.reference = Encounter/E-993355 and subject.identifier with MRN S3213957, plus the resource id after write.\n\nPlease proceed now and report back."
