      "content": "Thanks. Please perform the following for patient Victoria Owens (MRN S3236936, DOB 2002-06-07):\n\n1) Retrieve observations in the last 12 hours:\n- Pull the three most recent oxygen saturation results from:\n  - vital-signs category with code/text \u201cSpO2\u201d\n  - laboratory code/text \u201cO2SATA\u201d\n- Return for each: code, value and units, reference range/flag (e.g., LOW), timestamp, and whether it\u2019s a vital sign vs lab.\n\n2) Decision and order placement:\n- If the latest SpO2 is < 92% OR any O2SATA result is flagged \u201cLOW,\u201d then create a ServiceRequest with:\n  - intent = order\n  - priority = routine\n  - code.text = \u201cRespiratory therapy evaluation and oxygen titration\u201d\n  - subject.reference = Condition/38241 (Acute respiratory failure with hypoxia) \u2014 do not set this to Patient/S3236936. Route the order under this diagnosis.\n  - reasonReference = Condition/38241\n  - note = brief summary citing the triggering observation type (SpO2 or O2SATA), the value/flag, and its timestamp\n- Otherwise, do nothing.\n\n3) Report back:\n- List the observations you found (up to the three most recent for each type).\n- State whether the trigger criteria were met.\n- If an order was placed, provide the ServiceRequest ID and the exact subject.reference and reasonReference you used, along with the note text. If no order was placed, just confirm no action taken."
