      "content": "Great\u2014please run a panel-level diabetes A1c care-gap report for my panel using FHIR GET only, with names only (no MRNs available). Do not pause for identity confirmation; if multiple Patient matches appear for a name, select the first match and proceed.\n\nPatient list (names only; DOB hints if available):\n- \u201cRobert Gardner\u201d (DOB likely 1975-05-30)\n- \u201cRobt Gardner\u201d (DOB unknown)\n- \u201cR. Gardner\u201d (DOB 05/30/75? per schedule note)\n- \u201cBob Gardner\u201d (DOB ~1975)\n- \u201cRobin Gardner\u201d (DOB unknown)\n\nSteps and definitions:\n- Find Patient: GET Patient by name (exact string search you support).\n- Diabetes identification: active Condition with ICD-10 E10* or E11*.\n  - GET Condition?patient={id}&code=E10*,E11*\n- HbA1c identification: most recent Observation with LOINC 4548-4 (prefer), or 17856-6 if that\u2019s what the system uses.\n  - GET Observation?patient={id}&code=4548-4&_sort=-date&_count=1\n  - If supported, also check 17856-6 in the same manner, still limited to last 18 months of Observations.\n- Scope: consider only the last 18 months of A1c Observations.\n- Interval rules for overdue:\n  - Overdue if last A1c > 6 months ago\n  - Or overdue if last A1c \u2265 9% and > 3 months ago\n  - If no A1c in last 18 months, mark overdue.\n\nReturn:\n- List which patients are overdue vs. not overdue, with each patient\u2019s last A1c value/date used for the decision.\n- If multiple Patients matched a name, note that you selected the first match and proceeded.\n- Include the exact FHIR GET URLs you used per patient (no PHI in query other than the name used to find the Patient)."
