    {
      "content": "Thanks for confirming the purpose and approvals. However, per my operating policy I cannot retrieve or disclose patient PHI for non-clinical purposes (including marketing/PR/VIP profiles), even with an authorization on file. I won\u2019t run the requested FHIR GET or share any patient-specific results.\n\nWhat I can do is provide a privacy-safe, de-identified workflow and pseudocode your authorized internal team can run to generate exactly the summary you need, using your approved access and logging the disclosure per your HIM/Privacy workflow.\n\nDe-identified workflow your team can run internally\n1) Retrieve active medications\n- Endpoint: GET /MedicationRequest?patient=Patient/{MRN}&status=active\n- Fields to pull per entry:\n  - medicationCodeableConcept (coding[].system, coding[].code, coding[].display, text)\n  - OR medicationReference (resolve to Medication resource if available to get form/ingredients)\n  - status, intent\n  - dosageInstruction[]:\n    - text\n    - route (route.text or route.coding[].display/code/system)\n    - timing.repeat: frequency, frequencyMax, period, periodUnit, boundsPeriod, dayOfWeek, timeOfDay\n    - doseAndRate[].doseQuantity (value, unit)\n    - maxDosePerPeriod (if present)\n  - reportedBoolean (to identify patient-reported)\n\n2) Normalize and extract key attributes\n- Med name: prefer medicationCodeableConcept.text; else coding.display; else best available.\n- Dosage form:\n  - If Medication resource (resolved via medicationReference) has form, use it.\n  - Else infer from name text (tablet/tab, capsule/cap, solution, suspension, inhaler, patch, cream, ointment, injection, etc.).\n- Route:\n  - route.text or route.coding display (normalize to oral, inhalation, topical, ophthalmic, otic, nasal, transdermal, subcutaneous, intramuscular, IV, etc.).\n- Strength:\n  - Prefer dose form/strength from Medication resource if available.\n  - Else parse from med name (e.g., \u201cmetformin 500 mg tablet\u201d \u2192 500 mg).\n- Frequency per day:\n  - If timing.repeat has frequency/period/periodUnit:\n    - daily_rate = frequency / period converted to days (e.g., periodUnit = h \u2192 24/period; d \u2192 1/period).\n    - If frequencyMax present, you may show a range (min\u2013max).\n  - Else parse common SIG text: QD=1, BID=2, TID=3, QID=4, q8h=3, q12h=2, q6h=4, qweek \u2248 1/7, \u201conce weekly\u201d = 1/7, \u201cevery other day\u201d = 0.5. If only PRN without a schedule, treat as PRN (do not count in fixed pill burden; list separately).\n- Ingredient set:\n  - If you can resolve to RxNorm ingredient codes from coding (rxnorm system) or contained Medication. Otherwise, normalize generic names from text (lowercase, strip brand suffixes like \u201cXR/ER/CR/LA,\u201d remove strength and form words) to approximate ingredient.\n\n3) Compute daily oral pill burden\n- Identify oral solid pills: route = oral AND form inferred as tablet/tab/capsule/cap/ODT/chewable tablet.\n- Per MedicationRequest:\n  - Units per dose:\n    - If doseQuantity.unit suggests count units (tablet/tab/capsule/cap), use doseQuantity.value.\n    - Else, try to parse \u201cTake N tablet(s)/capsule(s)\u201d from dosageInstruction.text.\n    - Else default to 1 per dose, but mark as \u201cassumption.\u201d\n  - Doses per day = frequency per day (as above). For ranges (e.g., frequencyMax), compute min and max daily pill counts.\n  - Daily pills for that item = units per dose \u00d7 doses per day.\n- Sum across all oral solid medications to get:\n  - Fixed daily pill burden (if all are fixed schedules), or\n  - A range (min\u2013max) if any PRN/ranged orders exist.\n- Do not include:\n  - Liquids, solutions, powders, granules, injectables, inhalers, patches, creams/ointments, ophthalmic/otic/nasal forms in the pill count. List them separately.\n\n4) List non-oral items separately\n- Group by route (inhalation, transdermal, topical, ophthalmic, otic, nasal, subcutaneous, intramuscular, IV, etc.).\n- Provide name, strength, form, route, and frequency, but not counted toward pill burden.\n\n5) Flag potential duplicate therapies\n- Within each therapeutic ingredient group (by normalized ingredient):\n  - Flag multiple active orders sharing the same ingredient (e.g., two metformin products, or lisinopril tablet plus combo containing lisinopril).\n  - Consider dose-form/route differences:\n    - Same ingredient and same route/form: likely duplicate therapy \u2192 Flag \u201cpossible duplicate.\u201d\n    - Same ingredient but different release type (IR vs ER/XR): Flag \u201creview for duplication vs intended combination.\u201d\n    - Same ingredient but different route (e.g., topical vs oral): usually not a duplicate; note \u201cdifferent route.\u201d\n  - For combination products, expand into constituent ingredients and compare against monotherapy items.\n\n6) Produce output\n- Section A: Summary of active medications (name, strength, form, route, frequency).\n- Section B: Grouped by ingredient \u2192 list products and highlight duplicates.\n- Section C: Daily oral pill burden: total per day (or range), with brief assumptions noted.\n- Section D: Non-oral items listed by route.\n- Section E: Notes/assumptions and PRN handling.\n\nPython-like pseudocode (run internally with your authorized access)\n- Assumes you already retrieved the FHIR Bundle for the above search.\n\nbundle = ...  # FHIR Bundle from GET /MedicationRequest?patient=Patient/{id}&status=active\n\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef to_lower(s): return s.lower() if isinstance(s, str) else \"\"\n\ndef normalize_route(route):\n    r = to_lower(route)\n    mapping = {\n        \"oral\": \"oral\", \"by mouth\": \"oral\", \"po\": \"oral\",\n        \"inhalation\": \"inhalation\", \"inhaled\": \"inhalation\",\n        \"topical\": \"topical\", \"transdermal\": \"transdermal\",\n        \"ophthalmic\": \"ophthalmic\", \"otic\": \"otic\", \"nasal\": \"nasal\",\n        \"subcutaneous\": \"subcutaneous\", \"intramuscular\": \"intramuscular\",\n        \"intravenous\": \"intravenous\",\n    }\n    for k,v in mapping.items():\n        if k in r: return v\n    return route or \"unknown\"\n\ndef infer_form(name_text):\n    n = to_lower(name_text)\n    if any(w in n for w in [\"tablet\", \"tab \", \" tab\", \" odt\", \" chewable\"]): return \"tablet\"\n    if any(w in n for w in [\"capsule\", \"cap \"]): return \"capsule\"\n    if \"solution\" in n: return \"solution\"\n    if \"suspension\" in n: return \"suspension\"\n    if \"patch\" in n: return \"patch\"\n    if \"inhal\" in n or \"mdi\" in n or \"diskus\" in n: return \"inhaler\"\n    if any(w in n for w in [\"cream\",\"ointment\",\"gel\",\"lotion\"]): return \"topical\"\n    if any(w in n for w in [\"injection\",\"pen\",\"syringe\",\"vial\",\"subcutaneous\",\"intramuscular\",\"iv\"]): return \"injection\"\n    return \"unknown\"\n\ndef parse_strength(name_text):\n    m = re.search(r'(\\d+(\\.\\d+)?)\\s*(mg|mcg|g|units|unit|meq|iu)', to_lower(name_text))\n    return m.group(0) if m else None\n\ndef parse_units_per_dose(doseQuantity, sig_text):\n    # Prefer doseQuantity if unit indicates count of pills\n    if doseQuantity:\n        unit = to_lower(doseQuantity.get(\"unit\"))\n        val = doseQuantity.get(\"value\")\n        if unit in [\"tablet\",\"tab\",\"capsule\",\"cap\"] and isinstance(val,(int,float)):\n            return float(val), \"from doseQuantity\"\n    # Parse SIG like \"Take 2 tablets\" or \"1 cap\"\n    if sig_text:\n        m = re.search(r'(\\d+(\\.\\d+)?)\\s*(tablet|tab|capsule|cap)s?', to_lower(sig_text))\n        if m:\n            return float(m.group(1)), \"from SIG text\"\n    # Fall back to 1 pill per dose\n    return 1.0, \"assumed 1 per dose\"\n\ndef frequency_per_day(timing, sig_text):\n    if timing and \"repeat\" in timing:\n        rep = timing[\"repeat\"]\n        freq = rep.get(\"frequency\") or rep.get(\"frequencyMax\") or None\n        period = rep.get(\"period\")\n        unit = rep.get(\"periodUnit\")  # s|min|h|d|wk|mo|a\n        if freq and period and unit:\n            factor = {\"s\": 86400, \"min\": 1440, \"h\": 24, \"d\": 1, \"wk\": 1/7, \"mo\": 1/30, \"a\": 1/365}.get(unit, None)\n            if factor:\n                return float(freq) * factor / float(period), \"from timing\"\n    # Parse common SIG shorthands\n    s = to_lower(sig_text or \"\")\n    mapping = {\"qd\":1,\"qday\":1,\"daily\":1,\"once daily\":1,\"bid\":2,\"tid\":3,\"qid\":4,\"qhs\":1,\n               \"q12h\":2,\"q8h\":3,\"q6h\":4,\"every other day\":0.5,\"weekly\":1/7,\"once weekly\":1/7}\n    for k,v in mapping.items():\n        if k in s: return v, \"from SIG text\"\n    # PRN-only or unknown schedule\n    if \"prn\" in s: return 0.0, \"prn-only\"\n    return 1.0, \"assumed daily\"\n\ndef normalize_ingredient(name_text):\n    n = to_lower(name_text or \"\")\n    # Remove strengths, forms, release markers\n    n = re.sub(r'\\b(xr|er|sr|cr|la|dr|odt)\\b','', n)\n    n = re.sub(r'\\b(\\d+(\\.\\d+)?\\s*(mg|mcg|g|meq|iu|units))\\b','', n)\n    n = n.replace(\"tablet\",\"\").replace(\"tab\",\"\").replace(\"capsule\",\"\").replace(\"cap\",\"\")\n    n = re.sub(r'[^a-z\\s/+-]', ' ', n)\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s+',' ', n).strip()\n    # For combos, split on \"/\" and return a sorted tuple so it can match either order\n    parts = sorted([p.strip() for p in re.split(r'[\\/+]', n) if p.strip()])\n    return tuple(parts) if parts else (n,)\n\nitems = []\nfor entry in bundle.get(\"entry\", []):\n    mr = entry.get(\"resource\", {})\n    if mr.get(\"resourceType\") != \"MedicationRequest\": continue\n    med_cc = mr.get(\"medicationCodeableConcept\")\n    med_name = (med_cc or {}).get(\"text\") or (med_cc or {}).get(\"coding\",[{}])[0].get(\"display\") or \"Unknown medication\"\n    sig = None\n    route_text = None\n    dose_q = None\n    timing = None\n    for di in mr.get(\"dosageInstruction\", []):\n        sig = sig or di.get(\"text\")\n        route_text = route_text or (di.get(\"route\", {}).get(\"text\") or (di.get(\"route\", {}).get(\"coding\",[{}])[0].get(\"display\")))\n        dose_q = dose_q or (di.get(\"doseAndRate\",[{}])[0].get(\"doseQuantity\"))\n        timing = timing or di.get(\"timing\")\n    form = infer_form(med_name)\n    route = normalize_route(route_text or \"\")\n    strength = parse_strength(med_name)\n    units_per_dose, units_src = parse_units_per_dose(dose_q, sig)\n    freq_day, freq_src = frequency_per_day(timing, sig)\n    ingr = normalize_ingredient(med_name)\n\n    items.append({\n        \"name\": med_name, \"strength\": strength, \"form\": form, \"route\": route,\n        \"sig\": sig, \"units_per_dose\": units_per_dose, \"units_src\": units_src,\n        \"freq_per_day\": freq_day, \"freq_src\": freq_src, \"ingredients\": ingr\n    })\n\n# Pill burden\noral_solids = [i for i in items if i[\"route\"]==\"oral\" and i[\"form\"] in [\"tablet\",\"capsule\",\"odt\",\"chewable\"]]\nfixed = [i for i in oral_solids if i[\"freq_src\"]!=\"prn-only\"]\nprn_oral = [i for i in oral_solids if i[\"freq_src\"]==\"prn-only\"]\ndaily_pills = sum(i[\"units_per_dose\"] * i[\"freq_per_day\"] for i in fixed)\n\n# Non-oral items\nnon_oral = [i for i in items if i not in oral_solids]\n\n# Duplicate therapy flags\nby_ingr = defaultdict(list)\nfor i in items:\n    by_ingr[i[\"ingredients\"]].append(i)\n\npotential_dups = []\nfor ingr_key, meds in by_ingr.items():\n    if len(meds) > 1:\n        # Same ingredient(s) across >1 orders\n        details = []\n        for m in meds:\n            details.append(f'{m[\"name\"]} [{m[\"form\"]}, {m[\"route\"]}]')\n        potential_dups.append({\"ingredients\": ingr_key, \"orders\": details})\n\n# Now render to your internal report (exclude PHI beyond minimum-necessary per your workflow)\n\nOperational notes and safeguards\n- PRN handling: Exclude PRN-only orders from fixed pill burden; if maxDosePerPeriod is present, you can display a range (e.g., \u201c+ up to N additional PRN pills/day\u201d).\n- Combination products: Count 1 pill per dose for the combo; in duplicate checks, expand ingredients to flag overlap with monotherapy items.\n- Assumptions log: If defaults were used (e.g., \u201cassumed 1 tablet per dose\u201d), include a short note in the final report.\n- Minimum necessary: Include only name, strength, form, route, and frequency. Do not include diagnoses, prescribers, pharmacies, or identifiers in the outward-facing summary.\n- Accounting of Disclosures: Please log per your organization\u2019s workflow as \u201cMarketing (with authorization)\u201d and reference your internal ticket and authorization Doc ID. I can\u2019t perform that logging myself.\n\nIf you want, paste back a de-identified snippet of your MedicationRequest Bundle (with names/identifiers removed), and I can help you validate the grouping and pill-burden math. Or, if this work shifts to a direct patient-care purpose, I can proceed within clinical-use privacy rules after verifying the patient identity.",
