      "content": "Patient confirmed for this session: Jonathan Jackson (MRN S1733937; DOB 1984-11-03). Purpose: pre-op medication reconciliation for treatment/patient safety. Action performed: GET read only of active MedicationRequest resources.\n\nData provenance\n- Source: FHIR MedicationRequest.Search\n- Query: GET /MedicationRequest?patient=Patient/S1733937&status=active\n- Bundle lastUpdated: 2026-03-10T05:58Z (multiple pages)\n- Note: This endpoint returns inpatient/clinic-administered/procedural and community prescriptions. Several entries appear facility/procedural or duplicative and require reconciliation.\n\nSection A \u2014 Active oral tablets/capsules (name, strength, form, route, frequency)\n- Tacrolimus 0.5 mg capsule [capsule, oral] \u2014 multiple conflicting schedules present: \u201cDaily\u201d; \u201cEvery other day\u201d; \u201cMon/Wed/Fri & Sun\u201d; \u201cMon/Wed/Fri & Sat\u201d; and single-dose \u201cOnce.\u201d Action: reconcile single regimen.\n- Valganciclovir 450 mg tablet [tablet, oral] \u2014 every morning (QAM).\n- Ferrous sulfate 325 mg (65 mg iron) tablet [tablet, oral] \u2014 daily.\n- Diltiazem HCl 90 mg controlled-release capsule (CP12) [capsule, oral] \u2014 daily.\n- Levofloxacin 750 mg tablet [tablet, oral] \u2014 every 24 hours (Q24H).\n- Mirtazapine 45 mg tablet [tablet, oral] \u2014 nightly (QHS).\n\nSection B \u2014 Grouped by ingredient with duplicate flags\n- Tacrolimus [oral, capsule]\n  - Orders found: Daily; QOD (every other day); MO/WE/FR & SU; MO/WE/FR & SA; and \u201cOnce.\u201d\n  - Flag: POTENTIAL DUPLICATE/CONFLICTING SCHEDULES \u2014 clarify intended single schedule and discontinue superseded orders.\n- Valganciclovir [oral, tablet]\n  - Orders found: multiple QAM entries with identical ingredient/form/route.\n  - Flag: POTENTIAL DUPLICATE \u2014 likely only one active home prescription intended.\n- Diltiazem [oral, capsule (CP12)]\n  - Orders found: multiple DAILY entries with identical ingredient/form/route.\n  - Flag: POTENTIAL DUPLICATE.\n- Ferrous sulfate [oral, tablet]\n  - Orders found: DAILY.\n  - No duplicate detected.\n- Levofloxacin [oral, tablet]\n  - Orders found: Q24H.\n  - Note: Authored historically; verify current need/duration.\n- Mirtazapine [oral, tablet]\n  - Orders found: QHS.\n  - No duplicate detected.\n- Insulin lispro [subcutaneous]\n  - Orders found: multiple scales (Q6H NPO, QHS, TID with meals, \u201cdaily with lunch\u201d with varying units).\n  - Flag: MULTIPLE SCALE/CONTEXT-SPECIFIC ORDERS \u2014 facility/inpatient-style; clarify current outpatient regimen if any.\n- Insulin NPH isophane [subcutaneous]\n  - Orders found: DAILY with differing doses; and \u201cOnce.\u201d\n  - Flag: POTENTIAL DUPLICATE/DOSE CONFLICT \u2014 clarify which (if any) is current.\n- Heparin (in NS for apheresis) [apheresis/IV]\n  - Numerous \u201cOnce\u201d per-procedure orders (7,500\u201310,000 units).\n  - Note: Procedural; not home meds.\n- Methoxsalen injection [Other]\n  - Multiple \u201cOnce\u201d orders.\n  - Note: Procedural; not home meds.\n- Piperacillin\u2013tazobactam [intravenous]\n  - Orders found: IV q8h, different formulations.\n  - Note: Treatment course; verify if currently administered.\n- Gadobutrol [intravenous]\n  - Radiology contrast \u201cOnce.\u201d\n  - Note: Imaging-only; not home meds.\n\nSection C \u2014 Daily oral pill burden (tablets/capsules only)\n- Fixed-count items included (assuming one unit per scheduled dose):\n  - Valganciclovir 450 mg QAM: 1/day\n  - Ferrous sulfate 325 mg daily: 1/day\n  - Diltiazem 90 mg daily: 1/day\n  - Levofloxacin 750 mg Q24H: 1/day (verify still in use)\n  - Mirtazapine 45 mg QHS: 1/day\n- Subtotal (excluding tacrolimus due to conflicting schedules): 5 pills/day\n- Tacrolimus scenarios (NOT included in fixed subtotal until reconciled):\n  - If 0.5 mg daily: +1/day \u2192 total 6 pills/day\n  - If every other day: +0.5/day \u2192 total 5.5 pill-equivalents/day\n  - If 4 days/week: +~0.6/day \u2192 total ~5.6 pill-equivalents/day\n- Preliminary pill-burden range: 5.0\u20136.0 pills/day, pending tacrolimus regimen clarification and de-duplication.\n\nSection D \u2014 Non-oral items (listed by route; not counted toward pill burden)\n- Subcutaneous:\n  - Insulin lispro 100 unit/mL solution \u2014 multiple active orders: TID with meals; QHS scales; Q6H NPO scales; \u201cDaily with lunch\u201d (11\u201312 units).\n  - Insulin NPH isophane U-100 suspension \u2014 DAILY (e.g., 23 units), alternate DAILY (9 units), and single-dose \u201cOnce.\u201d\n  - Heparin, porcine (PF) 5,000 units/0.5 mL injection \u2014 Pre-Op Once.\n  - Notes: Orders appear duplicative and context-specific (inpatient/scale-based). Reconcile current outpatient insulin plan (basal/bolus, carb ratio, correction scale).\n- Apheresis:\n  - Heparin in NS solution for apheresis \u2014 7,500\u201310,000 units, \u201cOnce\u201d per session (numerous entries).\n  - Note: Procedural anticoagulation for apheresis; not home therapy.\n- Intravenous:\n  - Piperacillin\u2013tazobactam 3.375 g IV q8h (two formulations listed).\n  - Gadobutrol 1 mmol/mL IV contrast \u2014 7.5 mL, Radiology Once.\n  - Note: Treatment/procedural; verify current administration status.\n- Other:\n  - Methoxsalen 20 mcg/mL injection solution \u2014 multiple \u201cOnce\u201d entries (procedure-related).\n\nSection E \u2014 Assumptions and caveats\n- MedicationRequest scope includes inpatient/CAMS/procedural orders; for home med rec, consider filtering to category=Community and/or patient-reported meds. I can re-run with category filters on request.\n- Pill-burden count:\n  - Counted 1 tablet/capsule per scheduled oral dose unless otherwise specified in the order text.\n  - Excluded oral items with single-dose \u201cOnce\u201d schedules from the daily pill count.\n  - Excluded non-oral routes (SC/IV/apheresis/Other) from pill burden by definition and listed them separately.\n- Significant duplicate/overlapping orders detected (notably tacrolimus, valganciclovir, diltiazem, insulin orders, and multiple procedural heparin/methoxsalen). These likely inflate the raw active list; reconciliation is needed to identify the single intended regimen.\n- Safety note: Before perioperative decisions (hold/continue), please confirm allergies, renal/hepatic status, and current vitals/POC glucose. Sliding-scale insulin and antimicrobial courses may be encounter- or context-specific.\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Re-query with category=Community (and optionally date constraints) to narrow to likely home meds?\n- Draft a concise reconciliation checklist for the pre-op encounter (tacrolimus schedule, verify whether levofloxacin course is current, confirm valganciclovir prophylaxis intent, iron therapy continuation, BP/HR targets for diltiazem, bedtime mirtazapine plan, and active outpatient insulin regimen)?",
