2026-03-10 02:17:54 [INFO] Agent: Great—here’s a de-identified, synthetic walkthrough you can use for a resident teaching demo. Everything below is example-only (no PHI, not tied to a live EMR).

FHIR queries (read-only examples)

1) Retrieve last three BP panels (LOINC 85354-9)
- Standard FHIR approach (if code search and sorting are supported):
  GET {api_base}/Observation?patient={patient_id}&code=85354-9&_sort=-date&_count=3

- If your server requires the vitals category and you must filter client-side:
  GET {api_base}/Observation?category=vital-signs&patient={patient_id}&date=ge2023-01-01
  Then filter to Observation.code.coding where code == "85354-9" and extract component codes 8480-6 (SBP) and 8462-4 (DBP).

2) Retrieve active antihypertensive MedicationRequests
- Pull active meds, then filter client-side to antihypertensive classes (ACEi, ARB, thiazide, CCB, beta-blocker):
  GET {api_base}/MedicationRequest?patient={patient_id}&status=active
  Then match MedicationRequest.medicationCodeableConcept against a curated list (RxNorm/SNOMED or text-name matching) for:
  - ACE inhibitors (e.g., lisinopril, enalapril, benazepril)
  - ARBs (e.g., losartan, valsartan)
  - Thiazides (e.g., hydrochlorothiazide, chlorthalidone)
  - DHP CCBs (e.g., amlodipine, nifedipine)
  - Beta-blockers (e.g., metoprolol, atenolol, carvedilol)

