    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Great\u2014here\u2019s what I need you to do for Sarah Roberts (MRN S6212774, DOB 1960-02-28):\n\n1) Pull her Conditions. If needed to confirm CMV status, also pull recent lab Observations (e.g., CMV PCR/viral load, CMV IgM/IgG).\n2) Apply this referral rule:\n   - If ICD-10 D84.9 (Immunodeficiency, unspecified) AND Z94.2 (Lung transplant status) are present, OR if B25.9 (Cytomegaloviral disease) is present,\n   - Then create a ServiceRequest for a Transplant Infectious Disease consultation with:\n     \u2022 reason code: SNOMED CT 306206005 (\u201cReferral to infectious diseases service\u201d)\n     \u2022 priority: routine\n     \u2022 performerType: Infectious disease service\n3) After creating the order, check the payer portal and the in-network transplant ID specialist directory to:\n   - Identify an in-network transplant ID specialist with the earliest availability this week (prefer IU Health; if no in-network option this week at IU Health, use Eskenazi).\n   - Capture the specialist\u2019s NPI and clinic fax number and include both in the order notes.\n   - Obtain the payer pre-authorization ID from the payer portal and include it in the order notes.\n4) Route the order to the selected provider with the earliest availability this week.\n\nPlease report back with:\n- Which trigger codes you found (D84.9 + Z94.2 and/or B25.9)\n- The ServiceRequest ID you created\n- The selected specialist\u2019s name, NPI, clinic fax\n- The payer pre-auth ID\n- The earliest appointment slot you identified and routed to\n\nIf the referral rule is not met, let me know and stop."
    },
