      "content": "Here\u2019s what I was able to complete and what I could not retrieve:\n\nWhat I did\n- Created a new \u201csuperseding\u201d ServiceRequest for Sarah Roberts (MRN S6212774, DOB 1960-02-28) with:\n  - Code: SNOMED CT 306206005 \u201cReferral to infectious diseases service\u201d\n  - Status/Intent: active / order\n  - Priority: routine\n  - PerformerType: Infectious disease service\n  - Associated diagnosis (reasonCode): ICD-10 Z94.2 (Lung transplant status)\n  - OccurrenceDateTime: 2023-11-16T14:00:00-05:00\n  - Order note (entered exactly as you specified):\n    \u201cTransplant ID consult for lung transplant recipient (Z94.2) with recurrent infectious symptoms; evaluate for opportunistic infections and CMV risk. Please expedite for earliest availability this week.\n    Verified in-network via payer portal on 2023-11-13 10:35 ET; pre-auth ID: PA-IL-5792031.\n    Selected specialist: Alicia Nguyen, MD (NPI 1437289456); clinic fax 317-555-4820.\n    Scheduled earliest available appointment: Thu 2023-11-16 14:00 ET at IU Health Transplant ID Clinic.\n    This referral supersedes the earlier referral placed today.\u201d\n\nSystem responses and limitations\n- The create request succeeded, but the FHIR API did not return the created ServiceRequest resource or its ID. I attempted to retrieve it using:\n  - GET /ServiceRequest?patient=Patient/S6212774&code=http://snomed.info/sct|306206005&_sort=-_lastUpdated&_count=10\n  - GET /ServiceRequest?subject=Patient/S6212774&_sort=-_lastUpdated&_count=10\n  Both returned 0 results, so I cannot report the new ServiceRequest ID from this interface.\n- Setting a discrete performer by NPI is not supported in the provided POST schema; I could not set Dr. Nguyen as the performer. The detailed note and occurrenceDateTime have been included to support routing.\n\nRequested outputs\n- New ServiceRequest ID: Not retrievable via the current GET queries; please copy it from your EMR view if needed.\n- Confirmation note content: Added exactly as specified above.\n- Performer set: Not supported via this API; not set.\n\nNext step options\n- If you can share the ServiceRequest ID from your EMR, I can reference it going forward.\n- If a GET/Update (PUT/PATCH) ServiceRequest endpoint becomes available, I can pull the ID and update the performer field if supported by that endpoint.\n- Your scheduling/authorization staff can now route/schedule using the included specialist details, fax, pre-auth ID, and scheduled slot documented in the order note.",
