      "content": "Great\u2014thanks for getting the superseding referral placed and documenting the routing details.\n\nPlease complete and confirm the following so we can close the loop:\n\n1) Payer portal verification and confirmation reference\n- Re-check the payer portal to confirm PA-IL-5792031 is active as of today.\n- Capture the portal confirmation/reference number or transaction ID and the timestamp.\n- Add an addendum to the ServiceRequest note: \u201cPayer portal re-verified today; pre-auth PA-IL-5792031 active. Portal reference: [ID], [timestamp].\u201d\n\n2) In-network directory/NPPES verification\n- Verify Dr. Alicia Nguyen\u2019s in-network status, NPI (1437289456), clinic fax (317-555-4820), and practice address via the in-network specialist directory and/or NPPES.\n- Add source details to the ServiceRequest note addendum: \u201cIn-network directory/NPPES verified: NPI 1437289456; fax 317-555-4820; address 550 N. University Blvd, Indianapolis, IN. Source: [directory/NPPES link or reference], [timestamp].\u201d\n\n3) Scheduling confirmation\n- Confirm that Thu 2023-11-16 14:00 ET is still the earliest available slot this week for Transplant ID at IU Health.\n- If it has changed, rebook to the true earliest slot and update the occurrenceDateTime and note addendum accordingly.\n- Provide the appointment confirmation number.\n\n4) Routing/fax confirmation\n- Route the referral to Dr. Nguyen and send the referral packet via EMR eFax.\n- Provide the fax transmission confirmation ID and timestamp.\n\n5) ServiceRequest ID\n- Retrieve and report the ServiceRequest ID for the superseding referral. If FHIR search still returns 0, pull it from the order routing/scheduling log and share it here.\n\nIf any step is blocked by permissions, let me know exactly which ones so I can enable them. Otherwise, proceed and report back with:\n- ServiceRequest ID\n- Portal confirmation/reference ID for PA-IL-5792031\n- Directory/NPPES verification details (including link/refer