      "content": "Thanks \u2014 I\u2019m ready to close the loop, but I\u2019m blocked by missing capabilities. Here\u2019s exactly what I need enabled (or the data you can paste back) to complete each step:\n\n1) Retrieve and update the existing ServiceRequest\n- Needed to proceed:\n  - Read: GET /ServiceRequest search that returns the superseding referral for Patient/S6212774 (or the specific ServiceRequest ID if you can copy it from your EMR).\n  - Update: PUT or PATCH /ServiceRequest to append an addendum to note and (if supported) set performer.\n- Current status: My searches returned 0 results:\n  - GET /ServiceRequest?patient=Patient/S6212774&code=http://snomed.info/sct|306206005&_sort=-_lastUpdated&_count=10 \u2192 0\n  - GET /ServiceRequest?subject=Patient/S6212774&_sort=-_lastUpdated&_count=10 \u2192 0\n- Without read/update endpoints returning this resource, I can\u2019t add the required addendum or set a performer. If you share the ServiceRequest ID and enable PUT/PATCH, I will update the note exactly as requested.\n\n2) Payer portal verification (pre-auth PA-IL-5792031)\n- Needed to proceed:\n  - Access to the payer portal or an API that returns pre-auth status and a confirmation/transaction ID with timestamp.\n- Current status: No payer-portal access is available via these FHIR tools. If you provide the portal confirmation/reference ID and timestamp, I will add them in the ServiceRequest note addendum once update is enabled.\n\n3) In-network directory/NPPES verification (Dr. Alicia Nguyen, NPI 1437289456; fax 317-555-4820; address 550 N. University Blvd, Indianapolis, IN)\n- Needed to proceed:\n  - Access to the in-network specialist directory and/or NPPES (or an API/endpoint returning these source details), or you can paste the verification link/reference and timestamp.\n- Current status: No directory/NPPES access via these tools. If you provide the source link/reference and timestamp, I will add them in the addendum once update is enabled.\n\n4) Scheduling confirmation and rebooking if changed\n- Needed to proceed:\n  - Scheduling/Appointment API (e.g., GET/POST Appointment or EMR scheduling integration) to confirm or rebook and return an appointment confirmation number.\n- Current status: No scheduling endpoints are exposed here, so I can\u2019t confirm or rebook or obtain a confirmation number. If you share the final confirmed slot and confirmation number, I will document them in the addendum.\n\n5) Routing/fax confirmation\n- Needed to proceed:\n  - EMR routing functionality or a Communication/eFax API that returns a transmission confirmation ID and timestamp.\n- Current status: No eFax/routing endpoints are available. If you provide the fax transmission confirmation ID and timestamp, I will add them in the addendum once update is enabled.\n\nWhat I need from you to finish this now\n- Either enable these endpoints:\n  - GET /ServiceRequest (read)\n  - PUT or PATCH /ServiceRequest (update)\n  - Optional (to automate the rest): Payer portal API, Directory/NPPES API, Scheduling/Appointment API, Communication/eFax API\n- Or paste the following so I can immediately update the referral once PUT/PATCH is enabled:\n  - ServiceRequest ID:\n  - Payer portal confirmation/reference ID and timestamp (for PA-IL-5792031):\n  - Directory/NPPES source link/reference and timestamp for Dr. Nguyen\u2019s details:\n  - Appointment confirmation number and final date/time/location:\n  - Fax transmission confirmation ID and timestamp:\n\nAs soon as I have the ServiceRequest ID plus update permission, I will:\n- Append this addendum verbatim to the existing ServiceRequest note:\n  \u201cPayer portal re-verified today; pre-auth PA-IL-5792031 active. Portal reference: [ID], [timestamp].\n   In-network directory/NPPES verified: NPI 1437289456; fax 317-555-4820; address 550 N. University Blvd, Indianapolis, IN. Source: [directory/NPPES link or reference], [timestamp].\u201d\n- If supported, set performer to Dr. Alicia Nguyen, MD (NPI 14